  "title": "The bass clef",
  "summary": "The clef for the left hand, with its two dots round the F line.",
  "minutes": 6,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Bass clef",
      "body": "The **bass clef** is for lower notes. Its two dots sit either side of the fourth line, marking it as the F below middle C. Its lines from the bottom are G B D F A (\"Good Boys Do Fine Always\") and its spaces A C E G (\"All Cows Eat Grass\").\n\n**Why it matters:** Bass lines and the left-hand part of piano music are written in bass clef, so it is the clef that shows you what the bass player plays.",
